# .gitignore
.DS_Store
node_modules/
.env
scripts/
perfect_folder_looks.txt

# --- added 2026-07-26 (process-system scaffold) ---
# Secret hygiene. Every file in this repo is publicly served, so a leaked key is a
# published key. .env was already covered; these extend it.
#
# The `scripts/` rule above finally matches reality as of 2026-08-09: its one tracked
# file, scripts/data_collector.py, predated the rule and so stayed tracked and served
# while the rule implied otherwise. It is now untracked (LEDGER.md gitignore-hygiene,
# D-5). Two defects in the rules above still stand and need their own diffs: the
# gitignored build sources (`reproducible-build`) and the `perfect_folder_looks.txt`
# rule for a file that exists nowhere (`gitignore-hygiene`, D-4).
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.log

# Compiled Python bytecode from the .claude/hooks/ scripts. Untracked today, but a
# single `git add -A` would publish it — every file in this repo is served.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- added 2026-07-28 (local tool/editor noise) ---
# Per-machine Claude Code state that carries no project meaning. Untracked today;
# these rules stop a `git add -A` from publishing them. settings.local.json is
# already covered by the machine's global core.excludesFile — repeated here so the
# rule travels with the repo instead of living only on one laptop.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/*.local.json
.claude/todos/
.claude/shell-snapshots/
.claude/statsig/
.claude/history.jsonl

# Editor and OS byproducts. .DS_Store above already matches at any depth.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
Thumbs.db

# --- added 2026-08-09 (process system leaves the served tree) ---
# Every file in this repo is publicly served, so anything tracked here is published.
# The prompting/harness layer and the process documents are not part of the site and
# are no longer tracked: they were untracked with `git rm -r --cached` in the same
# commit that added these rules, which is what actually removes them from the served
# tree. A .gitignore line alone would not have — it does not affect tracked files.
#
# These files still exist on disk and still work; they are simply machine-local from
# here on. Older revisions remain reachable in git history up to that commit, but no
# future edit to them is versioned. That cost was weighed and accepted deliberately.
# If they ever need to be both unserved and versioned, the fix is structural — serve
# the site from a gh-pages branch or a docs/ folder — not a change to these rules.

# Prompting and harness machinery.
.claude/
loop-prompts/
references/

# Every markdown file. Nothing the site serves is markdown — every .md here is
# commentary for a reader, not content for a browser. This one rule subsumes the
# process documents (CLAUDE.md at all three levels, LEDGER.md, VERIFY-LATER.md)
# and the whole docs/ documentation tree.
*.md

# Except the root README — it is the repo's front page on GitHub, not commentary,
# and without it the repo page shows no description at all. Anchored to the root
# so it re-includes only this one file; references/README.md stays out, because a
# negation cannot re-include a file inside an already-excluded directory.
!/README.md

# The docs generator's resumability state. It is not markdown, so *.md never
# covered it, but it indexes only files that are now untracked — a listing of
# hashes for documents no clone will have. It belongs with them, not in the repo.
docs/_manifest.json

# Still tracked, deliberately: tools/ (repo tooling package.json invokes) and
# everything a browser needs.
